.TH EPIS 1 epis\-0.1.0
.SH NAME
epis \- small mail client with a vim-like interface
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B epis
.RB [ \-c
.IR config ]
.RB [ \-e
.IR commands ]
.RI [ command
.RI [ args ]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B epis
reads and sends mail. Without a command it starts the graphical client;
with a command it runs headless, which suits scripts, cron jobs and AI
agents. Mail is stored in Maildir folders under
.IR <maildir>/<account>/<folder> .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B setup
Interactive account setup in the terminal.
.TP
.BR sync " [\-a account] [\-f folder] [\-q]"
Two-way synchronization with the IMAP server.
.TP
.BR list " [\-a account] [\-f folder] [\-n N] [\-\-unread]"
List messages, newest first. Each line starts with the message id.
.TP
.BR search " [\-a account] [\-f folder] [\-\-body] query"
Search sender, recipients and subject, or bodies with \-\-body.
.TP
.BR read " [\-\-raw] [\-\-peek] id"
Print a message and mark it read unless \-\-peek is given.
.TP
.BR send " [\-a account] \-\-to addr [\-\-cc addr] [\-\-bcc addr] [\-\-subject s] [\-\-attach file]... [\-\-raw]"
Send standard input as the body, or as a complete message with \-\-raw.
.TP
.BR reply " [\-\-all] [\-\-send] id"
Build a reply with standard input above the quote; print it, or send it
with \-\-send.
.TP
.BR forward " \-\-to addr [\-\-send] id"
.TP
.BR flag " id [+|\-]flags"
Change Maildir flags: S seen, R replied, F flagged, T trashed, D draft.
.TP
.BR move " id folder", " delete id", " attachments id [\-\-save dir]"
.TP
.BR oauth " account"
Authorize an OAuth2 account (Gmail, Outlook) in the browser.
.TP
.BR autoconfig " email"
Discover server settings.
.TP
.BR llm " summarize id | draft id instructions | ask prompt"
Ask the configured language model.
.P
Every command accepts
.B \-\-json
for machine readable output.
.SH GRAPHICAL CLIENT
Keys follow vim. The leader key defaults to Space.
.TP
.B <leader>fi
find a folder (inbox)
.TP
.B <leader>fm
find a message by subject or sender
.TP
.B <leader>fc
run a command from a list
.TP
.B j k gg G <C-d> <C-u>
move in the message list or scroll a message
.TP
.B <CR> <S-CR>
open the message in this window or in a new window
.TP
.B r R f d a m s u
reply, reply all, forward, delete, archive, move, flag, toggle read
.TP
.B <C-w>v <C-w>s <C-w>hjkl <C-w>q <C-w>o
split side by side or stacked, move between, close and keep windows
.TP
.B <leader>c <leader>s <leader>a
compose, synchronize, summarize with the language model
.TP
.B v V
select text in a message (or drag with the mouse), then
.B y
to copy it
.TP
.B <C\-S\-c> <C\-S\-x> <C\-S\-v>
copy, cut and paste; Cmd\-C, Cmd\-X and Cmd\-V also work on macOS
.TP
.B :
command line, e.g. :move Archive, :attach ~/file.pdf, :send, :w, :q,
:!shell command (%f is the message file), :feedkeys keys,
:screenshot file.ppm
.P
.B \-e
runs ;-separated commands right after the window opens.
.P
On macOS the menus are in the system menu bar. Option types characters and
counts as Alt only with Control or with a non-printing key.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/epis/config
configuration, see epis.conf.example
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/epis/<account>.oauth
OAuth2 tokens
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B EPIS_TRACE
print the IMAP and SMTP dialogue to standard error
.TP
.B ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
API key for the llm commands when none is configured
